e01
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.440
Welcome to BuildTrack.

e02
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.650
If you run a construction company,
this will sound familiar:

e03
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.980
what was agreed gets lost in the chat,
invoices live in a box…

e04
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.800
and to find out where each project stands,
you have to call.

e05
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.850
BuildTrack brings it all together
in one place, from contract to closeout.

e06a
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.140
In the office: contracts, budgets,
invoices and payments.

e06b
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.090
You see where the money goes
before it eats your margin.

e07a
00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.600
On the jobsite, your crew clocks in
with a geofence,

e07b
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.210
even with no signal, and approved hours
go straight to payroll.

e08
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.570
And your client sees their project
through a link, nothing to install.

e09a
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.720
BuildTrack is built by ArchLogic Systems,
a team that comes from construction:

e09b
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:52.120
from budgets, payroll and site visits.

e09c1
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.410
And it's not a promise:

e09c2
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.340
it's already running
on real jobsites, today.

e10a
00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.880
It's for contractors with one to ten
projects, residential or commercial,

e10b
00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.220
who want order now,

e10c
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.800
not a six-month rollout.

e11
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.900
BuildTrack.
Run your jobsite without the chaos.
